course: dictionary
lesson: 11746
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which meaning the writer wants. «Mum is bagging the shopping at the till.» Shopping goes into bags, so bagging means putting things into bags. Always ask: which meaning fits these words?
explain: «Ben was bagging the best seat before anyone else arrived.» There are no shopping bags here. Bagging means getting or claiming something, so Ben grabbed the seat first. Check by swapping in your meaning: «Ben was getting the best seat» still makes sense.
explain: Look at what is being bagged. «Dad spent the afternoon bagging the leaves in the garden.» Leaves go into bags, so this bagging means putting them into bags. The clue is the thing next to the word.
fact: Bagging means putting things into bags, as in «bagging groceries».
fact: «Bagging a goal» means scoring a goal, so «She bagged two goals» means she scored two.
fact: «Bags I go first!» is a way children claim a turn.
fact: Bagging can also mean making fun of someone, as in «bagging on someone» in US slang.
fact: Bagging can be a noun meaning rough cloth used for making sacks.
exercise: «The cashier was bagging the shopping quickly.» What is bagging? | Winning a prize | Climbing a hill | Making fun of someone | *Putting things into bags
exercise: «Sam was bagging the last seat on the bus.» What does bagging mean here? | Sitting on a bus | Shouting loudly | Putting things into bags | *Grabbing or claiming something
exercise: «Maya bagged a goal in the last minute.» What does bagged mean? | Put in a bag | Lost | *Scored | Kicked the ball out
test: «Dad spent the morning bagging the leaves in the garden.» What does bagging mean here? | Burning | Singing | Scattering | *Putting into bags
test: «Ella bagged the front seat before the film started.» What does bagged mean? | *Claimed or got | Broke | Lost | Dropped
exam: In «Bags I go first!», what does bags mean? | I want to leave early | I am sorry I was late | *I claim the first turn | I am carrying a bag
